              "id": "CVE-2026-47675",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Hono: Cookie helper does not sanitize sameSite and priority, allowing Set-Cookie injection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.12.21, the serialize() function in hono/cookie validates domain and path options against characters that corrupt Set-Cookie header syntax (;, \\r, \\n), but does not apply the same validation to sameSite and priority. An application that passes user-controlled input into either option may produce a Set-Cookie response header containing attacker-chosen additional attributes. This vulnerability is fixed in 4.12.21."
